{
  "id": "secure-cicd-ecs-bluegreen",
  "category": "CI/CD & Developer Tools",
  "difficulty": "Advanced",
  "description": "A developer pushes to CodeCommit (pull requests to main need approvals). CodePipeline orchestrates the release: CodeBuild pulls pinned packages from CodeArtifact, reads Secrets Manager and Parameter Store, pushes an image tagged with the commit SHA to ECR and signs it with AWS Signer. CodeDeploy then shifts the ECS service blue/green behind the ALB, and a CloudWatch alarm on the ALB 5XX rate is attached to the deployment group for automatic rollback. ECR enhanced scanning sends Inspector findings to Security Hub; the application reads feature flags from AppConfig; CloudTrail records who deployed what.",
  "learningOutcome": "Select the Developer and choose git push (or Run pipeline on the pipeline). Then break it: set the developer to read-only, remove secretsmanager:GetSecretValue from the build role, fail CodeArtifact, or set the alarm to ALARM in the deployment group panel and watch CodeDeploy stop and roll back. Corrects common diagram mistakes: CodePipeline (not Signer) hands the build to CodeDeploy, and the alarm attaches to the deployment group, not to a Lambda alias.",
  "name": "Secure CI/CD: CodePipeline → CodeBuild → CodeDeploy ECS blue/green",
